# Word of Command (CR 723.2, 305.1-3): "to play a card" is to cast it or to play it as a land, and Bot2 may be made to
# play a land "if they have not already done so this turn" - in their own turn (CR 305.3), in any step (the effect is the
# permission, CR 608.2g). Bot1 casts Word of Command in Bot2's upkeep, looks at Bot2's hand (723.4: Looked) and chooses
# Brightclimb Pathway, both of whose faces are lands: which face is played is the controlled player's choice, so Bot1's,
# and it is Grimclimb Pathway. It is Bot2's land play for the turn (CR 305.2a): Bot2 can play no other in its main phase,
# and can again next turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Word of Command
Swamp x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Brightclimb Pathway
Mountain
Mountain x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Word of Command.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Brightclimb Pathway)
? Bot2.ControlledBy = Bot1
Bot2.Modes(Grimclimb Pathway)
? Bot2.ControlledBy = (absent)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
! Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Grimclimb Pathway.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 2
Bot1.Looked = Brightclimb Pathway; Mountain; Mountain; Mountain; Mountain; Mountain; Mountain
Bot2.ControlledBy = (absent)
